# Syncer

Obsidian plugin that syncs references/links to Google Tasks, Gmail Starred, Microsoft To Do, Outlook flagged mail, Azure DevOps work items, Firefox Bookmarks, and Todoist into a target Markdown note under a configurable heading.

## Start here

When changing behavior, read [`docs/kb/README.md`](docs/kb/README.md) and the relevant KB page before editing. Prefer code + KB over guessing sync rules.

## Project skills

Skills live under `.cursor/skills/<name>/`:

- [`update-knowledge-base`](.cursor/skills/update-knowledge-base/SKILL.md) — keep `docs/kb/` aligned after meaningful changes
- [`code-quality`](.cursor/skills/code-quality/SKILL.md) — layering, Zod, tests, project conventions
- [`sync-feature`](.cursor/skills/sync-feature/SKILL.md) — add or change a job/service/adaptor/auth integration

## Hard constraints

- Respect layers: no provider HTTP in `sync/`; no Obsidian APIs in `services/`
- Match existing conventions (Zod schemas, naming, British spelling)
- No new dependencies without explicit approval
- When sync semantics, architecture, conventions, or footguns change, update the matching `docs/kb/` page in the same task
- PRs that resolve issues must include `Closes #<issue>` (or `Refs #<issue>` when not closing), and post test evidence on the linked issue (PR link + automated results + manual verification notes) before merging
